  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Answer\\n\\n**Expect `InvalidCursorError` — Ordarium error code `INVALID_CURSOR`** (an `OrdariumError`, not a generic `LEDGER_*` failure).\\n\\n### What the failure is\\nThe pinned dependency line is **Ordarium 1.3.1** (`package.json` + `pnpm-workspace.yaml` pin `ordarium-v1.3.1` for core/ledger-sqlite/host-kit/testing). In that published contract:\\n\\n- `@ordarium/core` `errors.d.ts`/`errors.js` defines `InvalidCursorError extends OrdariumError` with `code = \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"` and message *\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point.\\\"*\\n- The documented trigger is exactly a **caller-supplied change-feed cursor that cannot be decoded as a durable position** (ORD-BOOT-0). \\\"Observation\\\" is the change-feed surface: `OrdariumStateStore.changes()` / `StateChangeFeed.changes()` is described as *\\\"incremental observation of committed state revisions after a durable position,\\\"* returning an always-present opaque `StateChangePage.cursor` — the position a consumer **stores** and feeds back.\\n- The SQLite reference ledger confirms the runtime behavior: `SqliteLedger.changes()` throws `InvalidCursorError` both when the cursor fails to decode and when",
